WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:01.622
Welcome to Captured.

2
00:00:01.899 --> 00:00:05.825
Good learning begins with preparation, so we start in Settings.

3
00:00:06.251 --> 00:00:08.875
Here you give your native language, your level,

4
00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:10.710
and the language you are studying.

5
00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:14.864
The tutor reads all three, and pitches every explanation to suit you.

6
00:00:14.986 --> 00:00:18.868
You also name your collections, verb tenses and grammar topics,

7
00:00:19.124 --> 00:00:21.766
so everything you add later already has its place.

8
00:00:22.716 --> 00:00:24.337
Now, vocabulary.

9
00:00:24.593 --> 00:00:29.201
Each word takes a definition, a source, and up to five collections,

10
00:00:29.457 --> 00:00:31.420
such as Food or Travel.

11
00:00:31.846 --> 00:00:35.820
In the reference field, double brackets link it to anything else you have saved.

12
00:00:36.081 --> 00:00:40.156
Phrases work the same way, with a literal meaning and an example.

13
00:00:40.476 --> 00:00:43.740
And all of it becomes flashcards, answered by typing,

14
00:00:43.975 --> 00:00:45.966
so your recall is properly tested.

15
00:00:46.783 --> 00:00:50.623
Verbs receive full conjugation tables, one column per tense,

16
00:00:50.836 --> 00:00:52.692
linked to the rules that govern them.

17
00:00:53.012 --> 00:00:55.743
Practice hides the forms: you fill in the table,

18
00:00:55.956 --> 00:00:58.620
check it, and any tense you miss comes back sooner.

19
00:00:59.483 --> 00:01:02.832
Grammar rules are built from text, tables and examples.

20
00:01:03.109 --> 00:01:07.440
Select any words in a rule, choose Link to, and they point to another rule,

21
00:01:07.547 --> 00:01:09.190
a verb, or a word.

22
00:01:10.050 --> 00:01:11.095
Why does this matter?

23
00:01:11.415 --> 00:01:13.548
Because nothing is learned in isolation.

24
00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:17.495
Every page shows what links to it, so a word leads to its rule,

25
00:01:17.730 --> 00:01:21.826
the rule to its verbs, and each review strengthens a network rather than a single

26
00:01:21.996 --> 00:01:22.295
fact.

27
00:01:23.317 --> 00:01:24.618
Then there is the tutor.

28
00:01:24.938 --> 00:01:27.903
Ask a grammar question, in English or in German,

29
00:01:28.053 --> 00:01:29.610
and it answers at your level.

30
00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:34.517
Every conversation is saved and searchable, and the tutor remembers what you discussed.

31
00:01:34.837 --> 00:01:37.153
Here is a long conversation on the dative case.

32
00:01:37.336 --> 00:01:40.344
Tick the answers worth keeping, make one rule from them,

33
00:01:40.451 --> 00:01:43.904
and save it to your grammar rules, linked to the rules it builds on.

34
00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:52.213
Finally, export everything to an Excel workbook or a JSON file,

35
00:01:52.383 --> 00:01:54.239
as a backup that stays yours.

36
00:01:54.687 --> 00:01:55.862
Viel Erfolg.
